IMPORT prelude

-- Cross-Border Railways Act 2018 (Singapore) -- what the Act decides for the people it most often touches: landowners near the
-- railway (entry on notice, ss 8 to 10, 12, 13; owner-initiated acquisition, ss 15, 16), passengers and members of the public at a
-- cross-border station (bag searches, s 61; endangering and damage, ss 62, 63; obstruction, ss 53, 64; identity, s 68), businesses
-- that run services on the line without authority (ss 25, 29), the compounding cap (s 73) and the first commencement (s 1(2) and
-- the commencement note).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (the deposit's page header reads "version in force from 30/9/2026"; its title
-- page says the revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/CBRA2018.txt. The latest amendment annotated is Act 16 of 2026 wef 30/09/2026 (ss 59 to 61, linked
-- to the Cross-Border Railways (Border Control Co-location) Act 2026); s 77 is annotated as repealed by Act 3 of 2021 wef 01/07/2025.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0093 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to the provisions an individual or a small business would meet. Not encoded: railway plans and maps (ss 4
-- to 6), State land (s 7), utility diversions (s 11), the Johore Straits bridge (s 14), funding (s 17), the concession, railway
-- assets and train service contracts (ss 18 to 24, 26 to 28), licensing (Part 6), monitoring (Part 7), opening and rights in land
-- (Part 8), safety audits and service suspension (ss 49 to 52, 54, 56, 57), security directives and agency powers (ss 58 to 60),
-- arrest (s 69), corporate and partnership liability (ss 71, 72), and the Land Acquisition Act 1966 sections that s 16 imports.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cross-Border Railways Act 2018 -- land and passengers`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` MEANS IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `1(2) and the commencement note -- what commenced on 14 September 2020`

-- Commencement note: "[14 September 2020: Parts 1, 2, 3, sections 21 to 24, 26, 27, 28, 65, 66, 67, 73 to 76, 78(1)(a), (b), (e),
-- (f) and (g), 78(2), (3) and (4), 79 and 80]".
-- s 1(2): "Sections 25 and 29, Parts 6 to 9 and sections 68 to 72, 77 and 78(c) come into operation on a date that the Minister
-- appoints by notification in the Gazette." The deposit records no later commencement date for them.
GIVEN `section number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section commenced on 14 September 2020` IF
        `section number` AT MOST 24
    OR  (`section number` AT LEAST 26 AND `section number` AT MOST 28)
    OR  (`section number` AT LEAST 65 AND `section number` AT MOST 67)
    OR  (`section number` AT LEAST 73 AND `section number` AT MOST 76)

§§ `8 to 10, 12 -- entry on land for the railway, and the notice owed`

-- s 8(3): LTA "must not exercise any power conferred by subsection (2) [enter private land and take possession] ... unless every
-- owner and occupier of the land is given at least 2 months' notice".
-- s 9(3): pre-construction survey of land gazetted under s 5 of the Land Acquisition Act 1966 -- "at least 14 days' notice".
-- s 10(3): inspection, survey and remedial work on land within the railway area "or within 150 metres" of it -- "at least 7 days'
-- notice"; (4) "However, subsection (3) does not apply if (a) the LTA is of the opinion that an emergency exists which necessitates
-- immediate entry; or (b) the entry is required only for the purpose of an inspection or a survey."
-- s 12(3)(c): a notice to remove a projection or obstruction must be given "not later than 28 days before" the removal period starts.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `taking possession of private land to build` -- s 8
    `a pre-construction survey` -- s 9
    `inspection or remedial work near the line` -- s 10
    `requiring removal of a projection` -- s 12

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the minimum notice in days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `a pre-construction survey` THEN 14
    WHEN `inspection or remedial work near the line` THEN 7
    WHEN `requiring removal of a projection` THEN 28
    OTHERWISE 0 -- s 8 is counted in months, below

-- s 10(2): (a) land or building "situated wholly or partly within the railway area"; (b) "wholly or partly within 150 metres of the
-- railway area".
GIVEN `partly inside the railway area` IS A BOOLEAN, `metres from the railway area` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the land is within reach of section 10` IF
    `partly inside the railway area` OR `metres from the railway area` AT MOST 150

GIVEN `LTA thinks it an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `only an inspection or survey` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 10 entry needs notice` IF
    (NOT `LTA thinks it an emergency`) AND (NOT `only an inspection or survey`)

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `days of notice` IS A NUMBER, `whole months of notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `LTA thinks it an emergency` IS A BOOLEAN, `only an inspection or survey` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice requirement is met` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `taking possession of private land to build` THEN `whole months of notice` AT LEAST 2
    WHEN `inspection or remedial work near the line` THEN
            (NOT `section 10 entry needs notice` `LTA thinks it an emergency` `only an inspection or survey`)
        OR  `days of notice` AT LEAST 7
    OTHERWISE `days of notice` AT LEAST `the minimum notice in days` `the power`

§§ `13 -- obstructing entry`

-- s 13(1): an authorised individual "must, if so required by the owner or occupier ... produce evidence of his or her authority
-- before so entering". (2) "Any person who refuses to give access to, or obstructs, hinders or delays, an individual authorised under
-- this Division ... shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $1,000."
-- Unlike ss 53(2) and 64(2), s 13 says nothing about what follows if the individual will not produce that evidence. The rule below
-- therefore does not read it as a defence; the flag is taken only so a test can show that.
GIVEN `refused access or obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the individual was authorised under Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `asked for evidence of authority and none produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obstructing entry is an offence under section 13` IF
    `refused access or obstructed` AND `the individual was authorised under Division 2`

§§ `15, 16 -- an owner may make the Government buy the land`

-- s 15(1): "The owner of any land possession of which is or has been taken in accordance with section 8 may, by written notice given
-- to the LTA, request the Government to acquire ... (a) the land; and (b) any other land of the owner related to the land ... if the
-- owner considers that he or she suffers substantial impairment of his or her rights". (2) "If there is more than one owner of the
-- land concerned, the notice ... must be given by all the owners." (3) "irrevocable once given".
-- (4) related land: "the remainder of a parcel of land part of which is the temporarily occupied land".
-- (5) "owner" means (a) fee simple; (b) "grantee or lessee under a State title"; (c) "entitled to exercise a power of sale"; (d) "a
-- person in occupation of the land under a tenancy the term of which exceeds 7 years".
-- s 16(1): the President "is to proceed under the Land Acquisition Act 1966 to acquire that land".
DECLARE Holding IS ONE OF
    `the fee simple`
    `a State title grant or lease`
    `a power of sale`
    `a tenancy in occupation`
    `a licence to occupy`

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding, `tenancy term in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holder is an owner for section 15` IF
    CONSIDER `the holding`
    WHEN `the fee simple` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a State title grant or lease` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a power of sale` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a tenancy in occupation` THEN `tenancy term in years` GREATER THAN 7
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding, `tenancy term in years` IS A NUMBER, `possession taken under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `considers rights substantially impaired` IS A BOOLEAN, `number of owners` IS A NUMBER, `owners joining the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may require acquisition` IF
        `the holder is an owner for section 15` `the holding` `tenancy term in years`
    AND `possession taken under section 8`
    AND `considers rights substantially impaired`
    AND `owners joining the notice` EQUALS `number of owners`

GIVEN `part of the same parcel as the occupied land` IS A BOOLEAN, `belongs to the same owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `other land may be included` IF
    `part of the same parcel as the occupied land` AND `belongs to the same owner`

-- s 16(2)(d): the Land Acquisition Act s 49A claim period is read as "one year starting from either of the following dates: (i) the
-- date of the notice under section 8 relating to that land; (ii) the date of the expiry of the term of possession ... or the date the
-- land is returned to the owner if earlier". READING (an inference): "either" is taken to mean a claim is in time if it falls within
-- one year of either date, so the later date governs in practice.
GIVEN `within a year of the section 8 notice` IS A BOOLEAN, `within a year of possession ending or the land being returned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the claim is within the claim period` IF
    `within a year of the section 8 notice` OR `within a year of possession ending or the land being returned`

§§ `61 -- bag searches at a cross-border station`

-- s 61(1): a railway official "may, without giving any reason, ask any individual in (a) a train station of a cross-border railway;
-- or (b) a cross-border train at a train station ... to allow the railway official to inspect and search any baggage ...; and that
-- individual must permit that baggage or thing to be inspected and searched." (2) an individual who refuses may be required "to leave
-- the train station or train, with that baggage or thing, and that individual must do so within a reasonable time." (3) contravening
-- (1) or (2) "without reasonable excuse" -- fine not exceeding $1,000.
-- (4) "railway official" means an individual "authorised by the cross-border railway security agency in writing": (a) an LTA officer;
-- (b) "a police officer or an auxiliary police officer in uniform"; (c) an employee of a licensee; (d) a security officer "engaged
-- by a licensee".
-- Leaving under (2) is "without prejudice to subsection (3)": the refusal is itself a contravention of (1), so leaving does not undo it.
DECLARE Asker IS ONE OF
    `an LTA officer`
    `a uniformed police officer`
    `a plain-clothes police officer`
    `a uniformed auxiliary police officer`
    `an employee of a licensee`
    `a security officer engaged by a licensee`
    `a security officer engaged by a station shop`

GIVEN `the asker` IS A Asker, `authorised in writing by the security agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the asker is a railway official` IF
    `authorised in writing by the security agency` AND
    CONSIDER `the asker`
    WHEN `a plain-clothes police officer` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a security officer engaged by a station shop` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the asker` IS A Asker, `authorised in writing by the security agency` IS A BOOLEAN, `at a cross-border station or train` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `refused the search` IS A BOOLEAN, `told to leave and did not within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual commits an offence under section 61` IF
        `the asker is a railway official` `the asker` `authorised in writing by the security agency`
    AND `at a cross-border station or train`
    AND (`refused the search` OR `told to leave and did not within a reasonable time`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `53, 64 -- obstructing inspectors, the security agency and railway officials`

-- s 64(1): refusing access to, or obstructing, the security agency, an authorised police officer or auxiliary police officer, or "a
-- railway official within the meaning of section 61" -- $5,000 or 6 months or both. (2) "However, it is not an offence ... to refuse
-- to comply with any request ... made or given by an out-of-uniform police officer or auxiliary police officer who fails to declare
-- his or her office and refuses to produce his or her identification card on demand".
-- s 53(2): the same carve-out for the independent safety auditor or a rail safety inspector, with no uniform condition.
DECLARE Official IS ONE OF
    `a uniformed officer`
    `an out-of-uniform police or auxiliary police officer`
    `a railway official who is not a police officer`
    `a rail safety inspector`

GIVEN `the official` IS A Official, `obstructed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the official failed to declare office and refused ID on demand` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `obstruction is an offence` IF
    `obstructed` AND
    CONSIDER `the official`
    WHEN `an out-of-uniform police or auxiliary police officer` THEN NOT `the official failed to declare office and refused ID on demand`
    WHEN `a rail safety inspector` THEN NOT `the official failed to declare office and refused ID on demand`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `68 -- evidence of identity`

-- s 68(1): a police officer or LTA employee "who reasonably believes that any person has committed an offence under this Act may
-- require the person to furnish evidence of his or her identity"; (2) refusing "or wilfully mis-states such information" -- $500.
GIVEN `officer reasonably believed an offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused or wilfully mis-stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `refusing identity is an offence` IF
    `officer reasonably believed an offence was committed` AND `refused or wilfully mis-stated`

§§ `13, 25, 29, 53, 55, 61 to 64, 68 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 13(2) $1,000. ss 25(2), 29(2) $50,000 or 6 months or both, and "in the case of a continuing offence, ... a further fine not
-- exceeding $5,000 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction". s 53(1) $5,000 or 6 months
-- or both; s 53(3) (failing to comply with a s 51 requirement, or false information) "$5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 6 months" -- NOT "or to both". s 55(3) failure by a "relevant person" to report an accident $100,000 or 5 years or both.
-- s 61(3) $1,000. s 62 wilfully endangering safety $10,000 or 5 years or both. s 63 wilfully removing, destroying or damaging "any
-- part of a cross-border railway" $200,000 or 12 months or both. s 64(1) $5,000 or 6 months or both. s 68(2) $500.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `obstructing land entry` -- s 13(2)
    `unauthorised open network services` -- s 25
    `unauthorised cross-border train service` -- s 29
    `obstructing a safety inspector` -- s 53(1)
    `false information to a safety inspector` -- s 53(3)
    `failing to report an accident` -- s 55(3)
    `refusing a bag search` -- s 61(3)
    `wilfully endangering safety` -- s 62
    `damaging the railway` -- s 63
    `obstructing the security agency` -- s 64(1)
    `refusing evidence of identity` -- s 68(2)

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `obstructing land entry` THEN 1000
    WHEN `unauthorised open network services` THEN 50000
    WHEN `unauthorised cross-border train service` THEN 50000
    WHEN `obstructing a safety inspector` THEN 5000
    WHEN `false information to a safety inspector` THEN 5000
    WHEN `failing to report an accident` THEN 100000
    WHEN `refusing a bag search` THEN 1000
    WHEN `wilfully endangering safety` THEN 10000
    WHEN `damaging the railway` THEN 200000
    WHEN `obstructing the security agency` THEN 5000
    WHEN `refusing evidence of identity` THEN 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `failing to report an accident` THEN 60
    WHEN `wilfully endangering safety` THEN 60
    WHEN `damaging the railway` THEN 12
    WHEN `unauthorised open network services` THEN 6
    WHEN `unauthorised cross-border train service` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing a safety inspector` THEN 6
    WHEN `false information to a safety inspector` THEN 6
    WHEN `obstructing the security agency` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `fine and imprisonment may both be imposed` IF
        `the maximum imprisonment in months` `the offence` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (NOT `the offence` EQUALS `false information to a safety inspector`)

-- ss 25(2), 29(2): the further daily fine, for each day "or part of a day" the offence continues after conviction.
GIVEN `days or part days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum further fine for a continuing unauthorised service` MEANS
    5000 TIMES `days or part days continuing after conviction`

§§ `73 -- composition`

-- s 73(1): the Chief Executive may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not exceeding the
-- lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b) $5,000." Which
-- offences are prescribed was not retrieved; the figure below is the cap IF the offence is prescribed.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap if prescribed` MEANS
    `the lower of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
